Wait for my YES or NO before adding it to the approved plan.

9. Always check whether a free GitHub Student Developer Pack alternative exists before recommending a technology or service.
10. Be concise when planning. For ordinary plans, target a maximum of 200 words unless I request a comprehensive document.
11. Explain technical instructions clearly, especially when I am working in Windows VS Code and PowerShell.
12. Do not expose secrets, passwords, API keys or database credentials.

## 4. CORE ARCHITECTURE — MULTI-TENANT SAAS

This is one platform, one codebase and multiple independent shop tenants.

Example:

- tailorly.com — Main Tailorly website.
- royalstitches.tailorly.com — Royal Stitches.
- elegantwear.tailorly.com — Elegant Wear.
- sammyfashion.tailorly.com — Sammy Fashion.
- tailorly.com/super-admin — Platform administration.

Each shop must have its own:

- Store name and branding.
- Logo and permitted theme customization.
- Products and collections.
- Customers and orders.
- Staff and permissions.
- Business settings.
- Messages and operational records.
- Reports and dashboard.

### Universal identity

One person must have one universal Tailorly account.

The same account can be:

- Shop owner in Shop A.
- Manager in Shop B.
- Customer in Shop C.

Roles and permissions must be specific to each tenant.

Never transfer privileges from one shop to another.

### Tenant isolation

Every tenant-owned database record must contain tenantId.

Resolve tenant identity from a validated hostname/domain mapping on the server.

Never trust a tenantId supplied by the browser as proof of tenant identity.

Enforce isolation across:

- Database queries and aggregations.
- APIs and server actions.
- Authentication and authorization.
- Background jobs.
- Caches.
- File uploads and downloads.
- Webhooks.
- Exports.
- Real-time messaging and Socket.IO rooms.

Test for cross-tenant data leakage, IDOR, unauthorized access and guessed identifiers.

Platform-scoped information, such as founder content, must remain separate from tenant-owned information.

## 5. SHOP SUBDOMAIN SYSTEM

The platform will use one primary domain with wildcard subdomains.

The domain registrar planned is Namecheap. Vercel is the preferred hosting direction, subject to current eligibility and deployment requirements.

Example:

- tailorly.com
- shopname.tailorly.com
- anothername.tailorly.com

The wildcard domain must be configured once at the DNS/hosting level.

Do not require the owner to manually configure DNS whenever a new shop joins.

### Shop creation workflow

1. Shop owner submits an application.
2. Owner verifies their email.
3. Application enters pending status.
4. Super Admin reviews the application.
5. Super Admin approves or rejects it.
6. On approval, Tailorly creates or activates the tenant.
7. A unique tenant subdomain is assigned.
8. The owner receives their shop URL and onboarding information.

Super Admin must also be able to create shops manually for invited or trusted owners.

Prevent duplicate and reserved subdomain names.

Unknown, suspended, pending and inactive shops must be handled appropriately.

Custom domains may be supported in a future phase.

## 6. DESIGN AND USER EXPERIENCE

Tailorly must look premium, professional, modern and trustworthy.

Design standard:

- Mobile-first.
- Responsive on phones, tablets and desktops.
- Clean and minimal layouts.
- Poppins or Inter typography.
- Consistent spacing and component design.
- Accessible contrast.
- Clear forms and navigation.
- Polished cards, dashboards and tables.
- Professional empty, loading and error states.
- Subtle animations only where useful.

### Official brand direction

- Navy: #173D78
- Cyan: #21B8C9
- White: #FFFFFF

Use these as the main brand colors, with restrained neutral backgrounds and borders.

Do not introduce additional major brand colors without approval.

The logo concept is an elegant T incorporating a sewing needle/thread. Final logo approval is still pending.

Include trust indicators, verified shop badges where verification is genuine, and a floating WhatsApp contact option where appropriate.

The quality target is to compete favourably with Bumpa and Flutterwave Store in usability and professional presentation.

## 7. HOMEPAGE REQUIREMENTS

The homepage must address both customers and shop owners.

Suggested headline:

"Discover Tailors. Find Your Style. Get It Made."

Primary CTA: Explore Shops.

Secondary CTA: Create Your Shop.

Include:

- Featured shops.
- Popular products and designs.
- Categories and collections.
- How Tailorly works.
- Benefits for customers.
- Benefits for tailors.
- Genuine customer reviews only.
- Trust and safety information.
- FAQs.
- Footer with contact and social links.

Customers must be able to explore public shops without applying to become shop owners.

